Release notes for balrogg. See ChangeLog for source-level changes.

v1.2 (06-09-2026)
- Accept Vorbis files without a final end-of-stream flag when the last
  packet is complete.
- Improve context mixer and Opus entropy coder performance.
- Support Unicode paths, arguments, long paths, and console output on
  modern Windows.
- Archives are incompatible with v1.1.

v1.1 (05-09-2026)
- Reduce memory use with file-backed, interleaved archive chunks and
  Vorbis model pages allocated only when used.
- Evaluate Vorbis tuning candidates over the whole file and retain the
  best encoded result without an extra encoding pass.
- Add encoding, decoding, and tuning progress with --progress and
  --progress-lines, including progress for batch jobs.
- Support padded and peeled Vorbis packets and alternative floor
  subclass choices while preserving the original bytes.
- Support extended Opus frame headers and padding, with packets up to
  61,440 bytes, including OpusHead and OpusTags.
- Archives are incompatible with v1.0.

v1.0 (03-09-2026)
- First release.
- Lossless Ogg Vorbis recompression with adaptive context models. Levels -5
  and above improve encoding without slowing decoding.
- Lossless Ogg Opus recompression using a parser derived from libopus. Each
  entropy-coded symbol uses its original probability table as a prior.
- Whole-stream and header-page deduplication for chained Vorbis files.
